.TH SAMEDAYDESK 1 "" "samedaydesk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.\" Generated from the command manifest; do not edit.
.SH NAME
samedaydesk \- SameDayDesk agent CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B samedaydesk
\fIcommand\fR [\fI\-\-flag value\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Noninteractive CLI for agents. One JSON envelope on stdout (samedaydesk.cli.result.v1 or samedaydesk.cli.error.v1), JSONL (samedaydesk.cli.stream.v1) when streaming, one diagnostic line on stderr on failure. No prompts. This version reads no credential and refuses secret\-named flags.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS discovery
Read this CLI's own command contract. Local, no network.
.TP
.B samedaydesk help [<group>]
Progressive help: groups, then one group's commands with usage. Effect: none. Auth: none. Retry: not_applicable. Recovery: rerun.
.TP
.B samedaydesk version
Package and manifest version. Effect: none. Auth: none. Retry: not_applicable. Recovery: rerun.
.TP
.B samedaydesk completion <shell>
Print a shell completion script generated from this manifest. Effect: none. Auth: none. Retry: not_applicable. Recovery: rerun.
.TP
.B samedaydesk commands [\-\-group <string>]
The complete command manifest. Effect: none. Auth: none. Retry: not_applicable. Recovery: rerun.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-group
Only commands in this group.
.RE
.TP
.B samedaydesk schema <command>
One command's inputs, output, effect, authority, route and recovery. Effect: none. Auth: none. Retry: not_applicable. Recovery: rerun.
.SS capabilities
Read current hosted capability, health and cost facts.
.TP
.B samedaydesk capabilities [\-\-origin <string>] [\-\-allow\-loopback] [\-\-dry\-run]
Gateway health and routes plus the market profile, each with its own status. Effect: read. Auth: none. Retry: bounded_get. Recovery: rerun.
